# 9/5/26 Moving in!
I've officially moved into my new apartment! The place is quite nice, I've never lived in a place this large before. It has some maintenance issues and needed *a lot* of cleaning when I moved in, but it's all things that can be solved :)

I'm not done setting up my room yet. So far it's looking like I'll have a lot of extra space left over even after moving everything in! I'll have plenty of space for experimenting with taking photos inside with my lighting equipment. It's still a mess in here though, and I'm on the hunt for a second desk. I'm hoping to get one of those desks that have shelves on it. I'll post images of my room once it's all set up!

I have a pretty sweet deal on internet at the new place too. My old place forced my to pay for xfinity internet (ew). Here I have gigabit fiber for only $45/month! And even better, I'm sharing my internet connection with my next door neighbours and splitting the cost between us. If I get to know my other neighbours better, I'll offer them in on the deal as well and maybe I'll be able to get it split 3 ways

Also the other day I got an email inviting me to the Illuminati lol:
![A screenshot of an email. The email is from "unosanthia@mopa.gov.bd" wit the subject "Join the illuminati.". The email reads "Are you interested in becoming a member of the illuminati brotherhood? Do you wish to be part of a group of like-minded people who striving to expand their knowledge and achieve personal growth? Or do you want to become wealthy? Resolve legal issues and become powerful and famous? If yes, contact us via this official recruitment email: contact@illuminatiinvite.com for more details. We look forward to hearing from you."](/resources/blog/9.5.26%20illuminati.png)

If I find myself really bored I might email them back and see where it goes haha. If you email them please tell me about it, I want to hear what the scam is exactly and what they say about "the illuminati"